Algorithm 1: Method Overloading in Python
Start.
Create a class named Addition.
Define a method add() with three parameters: a, b=0, and c=0.
Calculate the sum of the given parameters and print the result.
Create an object of the Addition class.
Call add() with one argument: 10.
Call add() with two arguments: 10, 20.
Call add() with three arguments: 10, 20, 30.
