Algorithm 2: Method Overriding in PythonStart.
Create a parent class named Parent.
Define a method show() in the parent class to print a parent class message.
Create a child class named Child that inherits from Parent.
Define a method show() in the child class with the same name as the parent method.
Print a child class message inside the child method.
Create an object of the Child class.
Call the show() method using the child object.
Display the child class message
Stop.
